<title>HONG KONG: HSBC shares could climb to HK$220 in '97.</title>
<headline>HSBC shares could climb to HK$220 in '97.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in HSBC Holdings Plc could climb to HK$220 this year, Raymond Lee, senior regional banks analyst at Lehman Brothers, said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>Lee told a presentation on the outlook for the Hong Kong banking and financial services sector that reaching that level would be totally reasonable and that the stock would benefit from a continued rerating from investors.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6345</p>
